 :30 pm) to Oct 1 (lunch) and a July 9\, 2027 abstract deadline\; the Abst
 racts tab header says Sep 27-30. No cutoff hour is published\, so 23:59 A
 oE is provisional. Abstracts are submitted via an emailed link after regi
 stering\; organizers pick talks and posters\, and presenters should atten
 d in person (Zoom/virtual packages for others). Abstract texts appear onl
 y in the confidential program book. 2024 listed 140 accepted abstracts (3
 3 talks) plus 20 invited speakers. Size is an editorial estimate.
CATEGORIES:Neuromorphic & Brain-inspired Computing,Computational Neuroscien
 ce,Machine Learning,Deep Representation Learning
